This appears to be a CBP ruling on Graybond products. Candidates are 3824.50 (ready-mixed concrete/mortars), 3824.99 (chemical products and preparations of the chemical or allied industries, n.e.s.), and 2523.90 (other hydraulic cements). The items have no cementitious value on their own, so they are not hydraulic cements under 2523. A mixture of pozzolan and limestone, some with quicklime, fits 3824.99 as a chemical preparation not elsewhere specified. Graybond 4BF has no quicklime, but the same heading applies.

The subheading is 3824.99, and the statistical suffix for "other" under 3824.99 is 3824.99.9295 (other, not elsewhere specified). Plausible alternatives are 3824.99.2800 and 3824.99.9290, but I am choosing 3824.99.9295 as the best fit.

{"hts_code": "3824.99.9295", "reason": "Non-cementitious blends of pozzolan, limestone and (in some cases) quicklime are chemical mixtures not elsewhere specified, so they fall in heading 3824 rather than hydraulic cements of heading 2523."}
